// THE ONE-ARMED VETERAN (Corey, 2026-10-08) - he stands at the Edgeville side of the ditch and has
// nothing to sell. He is the one who tells you what the Undertaker is for.
//
// HIS ARM IS ACTUALLY GONE, not implied by his name. A *_manwear2 model is the pair of sleeves,
// symmetric about the body's middle, so every face lying wholly on one side of it was dropped; the
// platebody's pauldron on that side went with it, because with the pauldron left on a 377 figure
// reads as a man standing square on and the missing arm cannot be seen at all. The faces that
// straddle the middle are kept, so the chest is whole.
//
// Tinted one part at a time, like the Undertaker, so the walk and ready animations still have the
// vertex labels they deform (a merged figure has none and slides about in a T-pose).
[wilderness_veteran]
name=One-armed veteran
desc=He has been to the places you are about to go.
model1=npc_veteran_helm
model2=idk_42
model3=idk_man_jaw_short
model4=npc_veteran_body
model5=npc_veteran_arm
model6=npc_veteran_legs
model7=npc_veteran_cape
model8=npc_veteran_boots
head1=idk_man_jaw_short_head
readyanim=human_ready
walkanim=human_walk_f,human_walk_b,human_walk_l,human_walk_r
vislevel=hide
wanderrange=0
op1=Talk-to
